# Burp Suite Proxy Configuration

## Objective

Learn how to configure Burp Suite as an intercepting proxy between Firefox and OWASP Juice Shop to capture and inspect HTTP requests.

---

## Overview

Burp Suite is an intercepting proxy used by Application Security Engineers and Penetration Testers to inspect, modify, and analyze web traffic between a browser and a web application.

---

## Lab Environment

* Host OS: Windows 11
* Guest OS: Kali Linux
* Virtualization: VMware / VirtualBox
* Docker
* OWASP Juice Shop
* Burp Suite Community Edition
* Mozilla Firefox

---

## Prerequisites

* Docker installed and running
* OWASP Juice Shop container running
* Juice Shop accessible at:

```text
http://localhost:3000
```

---

## Network Flow

```text
Firefox
    │
    ▼
Burp Suite (Intercepting Proxy)
    │
    ▼
OWASP Juice Shop
```

---

## Lab Tasks

* Launch Burp Suite.
* Create a Temporary Project.
* Select **Use Burp Defaults**.
* Configure Firefox to use Burp Suite as its proxy.
* Enable request interception.
* Capture the first HTTP request.
* Analyze the intercepted request.

---

## Firefox Proxy Configuration

| Setting                          | Value     |
| -------------------------------- | --------- |
| HTTP Proxy                       | 127.0.0.1 |
| Port                             | 8080      |
| Use this proxy for all protocols | Enabled   |

---

## Expected HTTP Request

```http
GET / HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:3000
```

---

## Learning Objectives

* Understand the purpose of an intercepting proxy.
* Learn how browser traffic flows through Burp Suite.
* Capture and inspect HTTP requests.
* Prepare the environment for future Application Security testing.

